WHAT’S IN THE LEAF<br><small>ALKALOIDS, MITRAGYNINE &amp; WHY MILLIGRAMS MATTER</small>
</h2>
<div class="ak-prose ak-prose-wide">
<p class="ak-lead">
Kratom leaves contain more than 40 naturally occurring plant compounds called <strong>alkaloids</strong>. The most abundant, studied, and important alkaloid is <strong>mitragynine</strong>.
</p>
<p>
Mitragynine is the engine behind kratom’s benefits. It is responsible for the alert focus you feel at lower amounts and the physical relaxation you experience at higher ones.
</p>
<p>
But here is the problem with the unregulated kratom market: most vendors sell anonymous bags of powder stamped with made-up strain names like "Super Platinum Dragon." You never know how much active mitragynine is actually inside, which makes finding a consistent routine nearly impossible.
</p>
</div>
<div class="ak-pillars">
